.claude/i18n-strings-checked
.claude/wiki-recompact-pending

# GAIA release/update working directories
# No trailing slash: in the main checkout this is a directory, in a provisioned
# worktree it is a symlink to that directory. The slash form matches only the first.
.gaia/local
# The linker never clobbers: it moves whatever already sits at the path it is
# about to link to `<path>.bak.<timestamp>`. Since the linked path is
# `.gaia/local` itself, that backup is its sibling rather than its child, so
# the line above does not cover it and the local state it holds would otherwise
# be stageable.
.gaia/local.bak.*
.gaia/statusline/.use-vendored-base
.gaia-backup/
.gaia-merge/


# Scratch copies of .gaia/tests/bats-shards.sh that its guard suite doctors in
# place. They live inside the repo because the sharder derives its own repo
# root from git, which fails from outside a working tree. teardown() removes
# them; this entry covers an interrupted run, where teardown never fires.
.bats-shards-scratch.*
